  "reviewNotes": "PDF page7; native front/back source views. Source379990triangles/18999584bytes,max49.828999mm. Same1x1 footprint and17mm native insertion shoulder as35; measured centre floor24.728354mm. Both faces have diagonal bracing. Direct comparison to35 shows median .455mm change across plaster, so nearest-source difference is not a valid material mask here. Fit actual beam cores: front x>-10.85mm yields780vertices andYZ axis[.789239,.614086], rear x<-17.2 yields1216vertices andaxis[.795893,.605438]. Native transverse ranges[-2.349,2.248]/[-2.463,1.979]mm gain .4mm for curved flanks. Front timber boundedx[-11.35,-10.25],rear[-17.55,-16.65], with individual projections; exclude these exact regions from both-face ochre plaster. Preserve X floor boards, Y frame/fascia, Z posts and two oblique grains. Wall remainswest edge/64 withlocalX0..0.22 blocker; centre point must match source/render/LOD. Review complete brace flanks and contact edges in both tiers/candidates before publication. Render UV .35rad/.0012 passed, but LOD overlapped surfaces .759mm apart. Recreate LOD at.25rad/.0008 margin and rebake both reports before acceptance. Balanced passed UV and complete material checks; compact768px render had .227mm physical collision and is rejected without weakening .1mm tolerance. Initial thin X ranges left a plaster-coloured side face on the front brace: expand front depth to[-13.4,-10.25] and rear[-17.55,-14] according to actual protruding sculpt bounds (-12.9772front/-14.4482rear) plus contact margin. Keep both YZ projections and separate wall faces.",
